---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// In-site links must carry the base (/agentviz) prefix.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const linkClass = 'text-sky-400 transition-colors hover:text-sky-300';
---

<Base
	title="About"
	description="What AgentViz is for: turning the invisible API calls, agent loops, and data flows of AI application development into animations."
	locale="en"
>
	<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">About</h1>
	<p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
		AgentViz turns the invisible parts of building AI applications — API calls, agent loops, and
		data flows — into animations you can play, step through, and take apart.
	</p>
	<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
		What this site draws is the layer underneath your application code: how a request gets packed,
		how a tool call round-trips, how retrieval becomes a pipeline. Every lesson comes with a demo you
		can push around — play it, single-step it, click any event for its detail. Think of it as an
		architecture diagram that moves.
	</p>
	<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
		The site itself is one practice of the same idea: a static build, no backend, no tracking, every
		interaction running in the browser. The numbers in the lessons are teaching data you can recompute
		by hand, the references are official documentation only, and every lesson lists its sources at the
		bottom so they can be checked.
	</p>

	<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Who it's for</h2>
	<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
		Written for developers with any engineering background. No algorithms or machine-learning
		experience is assumed — being able to read a call stack is enough. The systems analogies in the
		prose lean on C++/Qt (signals and slots, the message loop) only as a way to make "callback" and
		"event queue" concrete; if you come from the front end, Promise, fetch, and the event loop line
		up with them, and nothing in the argument depends on which of the two you happen to know.
	</p>

	<h2 class="mt-10 text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100">Chinese-only pages</h2>
	<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
		The full-screen sandboxes and the aggregated source index have not been translated yet — both are
		currently published in Chinese only:
		{' '}
		<a href={`${base}/lab/`} class={linkClass}>实验室 (Lab)</a>
		{' '}and{' '}
		<a href={`${base}/references/`} class={linkClass}>参考库 (References)</a>.
	</p>

	<p class="mt-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
		Spotted something stated wrongly? Open an issue on the
		{' '}
		<a
			href="https://github.com/classkow/agentviz"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
			class={linkClass}>GitHub repository</a
		>.
	</p>
</Base>
